  "body": "## What changed\n\nTwo site pages said that the browser version cannot open or save files. This is not correct since v0.20.0.\n\n- `site/templates/index.html`: the front page paragraph about the browser version.\n- `site/content/guide/first-run.md`: the paragraph \"Trying it in the browser first\".\n\nThe pages now say:\n\n- The browser version opens a model or a project with the file picker of the browser (PR #1314).\n- Save and Save As download the project (PR #1438). Post downloads the program when Output is set to one combined program. One file for each operation is refused (`browser_files::refusal`).\n- The other file commands are greyed, or refused with the reason on the status line (the theme picker is not greyed). The list follows `browser_files::refusal` in `crates/ui/src/browser_files.rs`.\n\n## Readings\n\n- `RELEASE_NOTES.md` for v0.20.0 already says: \"The browser build opens files with a picker, saves, and posts as downloads\".\n- The merge commit of PR #1314 is an ancestor of the tag `v0.20.0`.\n\n## Tests\n\nNo test pins this text. The change is text only.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The site was not built with zola. The edit changes no template syntax.\n- The text no longer says anything about simulation playback in the browser. The code does not confirm a limit. A new sentence needs a check in the browser build first.\n- Nobody opened the browser version to try the commands.\n\nChangelog: none\n\nFixes #1833\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n",
